 check --no-default-features                        OK\n--- cargo check --all-features                               OK\n\n=== release cdylib | (default)                           PASS (55 tests)\n=== release cdylib | --no-default-features               PASS (55 tests)\n=== release cdylib | --all-features                      PASS (55 tests)\n\n=== debug cdylib   | (default)                           PASS (55 tests)\n=== debug cdylib   | --no-default-features               PASS (55 tests)\n=== debug cdylib   | --all-features                      PASS (55 tests)\n\nALL FEATURE COMBINATIONS PASSED\n\n=== final artifact listing ===\nCONFIGS.md\nERRORS.md\nSYMBOLS.md\nVERIFICATION.md\ncheck_all_features.sh\nmutation_check.sh\n\ntests/:\ncommon\nphase_b_valid.rs\nphase_c_errors.rs\nphase_d_build_sensitivity.rs\nphase_d_symbols.rs\n\ntests/common/:\nmod.rs\n\n=== symbol parity ===\nEMPTY","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ece6iud2kyfpujcsewp6zjjzpg3vzbxnunwp2gctibjablznkpla","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All phases complete and independently verified.\n\n## Result: the translation is correct — no changes to `src/lib.rs` were needed\n\nThe library is small (one exported symbol, 29 lines of C), so the work went into proving the *hard* part rather than covering more surface.\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (`SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`) — derived by mechanically grepping the C, not from assumptions. The grep found **zero** `if`/`switch`/`assert`/`return -1`/`enum`/pointer/`malloc`/`#ifdef` constructs: this API has no validation and no error channel at all, so its entire error surface is IEEE-754 exceptional conditions reachable through the unguarded `1.0f / (dot00*dot11 - dot01*dot01)`.\n\n**Phases B–D** — 55 tests, ~2.6 M randomised comparisons per feature combo, both libraries loaded via `libloading` and compared as raw `u32` bit patterns (so `±0.0` and NaN payloads both count). `nm -D` diff is empty; 6 configurations (3 feature combos × release/debug cdylib) all pass.\n\nThree things worth flagging:\n\n1. **I validated the tests, not just ran them.** `mutation_check.sh` injects 20 deliberate divergences. 15 observable ones are caught; **5 survive — and they provably cannot be caught**, each with a proof in `ERRORS.md`. E.g. the denominator's `dot00*dot11` operand order is unobservable because if both are NaN, the numerators start with `mul_dst_lhs(dot11, dot02)` / `mul_dst_lhs(dot00, dot12)`, whose NaN left operand wins the subsequent `subss` and `mulss` — masking `invDenom` entirely. These are equivalent mutants, not gaps, but the distinction only became visible by running them.\n\n2. **The NaN payload belongs to the reference *binary*, not the C source.** Two builds of the identical `lib.c` agree on 200 000/200 000 NaN-free inputs but disagree on **186 698/200 000** NaN-carrying ones. `CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so the reference is `-O0`; Rust matches it on all 293 439 sampled inputs where `-O2` answers differently. Stated plainly in `VERIFICATION.md`: multi-NaN bit-exactness holds against the build `CMakeLists.txt` produces, and *cannot* hold against an arbitrarily-optimised build — the C does not agree with itself there. Test `d9` fails with an explanation if the reference build ever gains `-O` flags.\n\n3. **A correction to my own draft.** `ERRORS.md` initially claimed exactly-collinear triangles could yield `±inf`. Measurement showed they always yield `0xFFC0_0000`: substituting `v0 = t·v1` makes both numerators vanish exactly, so it is `0 * inf`, not `x/0`. `±inf` only arises when *rounding* zeroes the denominator while a numerator survives. I found witnesses for that and for a negative denominator (which produces `-0.0` — invisible to a non-bitwise comparison) and pinned both as literals.\n\nI also fixed a genuine race I introduced: `d7` and `d8` were concurrently `gcc -o`-ing the same path, which flaked once. Now built once behind a `OnceLock` with atomic rename; 5 consecutive clean-slate runs pass.\n\nOne caveat on scope: `cargo test` alone does not emit a cdylib for a `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` crate, so the harness shells out to `cargo build` in a side target dir. I did not change `crate-type` to add `rlib`, deliberately — that would have let integration tests link the crate directly, defeating the requirement to go through `dlsym`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":974,"cache_read_input_tokens":162891,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":974,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ed20977-f5f8-4deb-9a86-a926773132a1","uuid":"74c75358-e29f-44f8-9119-ff9032cf9197","timestamp":"2026-08-27T02:04:29.809Z"}
